From 5e52efbef4c699f8beaf5f7835adc0f8f3371263 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:01:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(post): machine files for the PCNC 770 and PCNC 1100
 from their manuals

Four inch machine files, each built from the Specifications section of
its own Tormach operator's manual:

- Tormach PCNC 770 (Series 3): 32426 Rev C1-1. Rapids are 135/100 IPM.
  The earlier B1-4 manual says 130 IPM for X/Y, and the later revision
  wins.
- Tormach PCNC 1100 (Series I): 30625 Rev C4-1, 300-4500 rpm, 65 IPM.
- Tormach PCNC 1100 (Series II): 31138 Rev B1-4, 100-5140 rpm, 90/65 IPM.
- Tormach PCNC 1100 (Series 3): UM10087 1013A, 100-5140 rpm, 110/90 IPM.

Each file states both belt ranges and the rated motor power (not the
peak), plus Flood M8 and Mist M7. Each also sets rigid_tapping false:
these are R8 mills that tap with the M871-M874 tapping-head macros, so
the Tormach post refuses a G84 on them by name.

All four are registered in posting::MACHINES and pinned in
tests/machine.rs and tests/tormach_machines.rs (figures, belt notes,
tap refusal). Sources, pages and the 770 disagreement are recorded in
docs/decisions/170-tormach-pcnc.md.

Refs #170

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
